# Per-Service `tsconfig.json` — Mandatory Paths Override

## The Trap

The root [`tsconfig.json`](../../tsconfig.json) sets `"baseUrl": "."` (the repo root) and
maps every internal package to its **source** directory:

```json
"paths": {
  "@ente-doctor/common":    ["packages/common/src"],
  "@ente-doctor/contracts": ["packages/contracts/src"],
  "@ente-doctor/event-bus": ["packages/event-bus/src"]
}
```

When a service `tsconfig.json` extends the root without overriding these fields, TypeScript
resolves `@ente-doctor/common` to `packages/common/src/index.ts`. That file lives **outside**
the service's own `rootDir: "src"`, which causes:

```
TS6059: File '…/packages/common/src/index.ts' is not under 'rootDir' '…/apps/<service>/src'.
```

This breaks `tsc --noEmit` (the `lint` script) in every service that imports an internal package.

## Canonical Per-Service `tsconfig.json`

Every file at `apps/<service>/tsconfig.json` **must** look exactly like this:

```json
{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": "dist",
    "rootDir": "src",
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "dist/.tsbuildinfo",
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {}
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "**/*.spec.ts"]
}
```

## Two Mandatory Invariants

1. **`"baseUrl": "."`** — must be present. Overrides the repo-root `baseUrl` so the service
   resolves non-relative imports from its own directory, not the repo root.

2. **`"paths": {}`** — must be present and **empty**. An empty object clears the inherited
   `@ente-doctor/*` source mappings, forcing TypeScript to resolve those packages through
   `node_modules`. Node modules resolution then hits the compiled `dist/index.d.ts` declared
   in each package's `"types"` field — not the source `.ts` file.

Omitting **either** field re-inherits the root mapping and triggers TS6059.

## Prerequisite — Shared Package `dist/` Must Exist

Before running `corepack pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/<service> lint` or `build`, the three
shared packages must already have a compiled `dist/`. If they have never been built (or were
cleaned), run:

```powershell
corepack pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/common build
corepack pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/contracts build
corepack pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/event-bus build
```

These are cheap (< 5 s each). A single `corepack pnpm install` after building refreshes the
workspace symlinks so every service sees the compiled output.

## Reference — Correctly Configured Services

Both `apps/auth-service/tsconfig.json` and `apps/notification-service/tsconfig.json` already
carry the override. Use either as a copy-paste reference when bootstrapping a new service.

## Checklist When Adding a New Service

- [ ] `apps/<service>/tsconfig.json` contains `"baseUrl": "."` and `"paths": {}`
- [ ] Shared packages have a built `dist/` (`corepack pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/<pkg> build`)
- [ ] `corepack pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/<service> lint` exits 0 before the first commit
